WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.039
[Description] Over Justin's shoulder as he sits at a large monitor showing a website. On-screen

00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:07.727
title: “What makes a website inaccessible?”

00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:10.217
So we're going to talk about things that are not

00:00:10.217 --> 00:00:13.737
accessible. It's not necessarily just a lack of trying. A

00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:15.857
lot of the times, people just don't know. So, no

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:18.137
disrespect, but, like, this kind of thing is frustrating.

00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:20.694
[Description] Justin magnifies the site's menu until the word “NEWS” fills the screen in dark

00:00:20.694 --> 00:00:23.251
text on white.

00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:28.411
Like, this level of contrast is fantastic. This black on

00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:32.210
white background, it's easy to see. But usually then I

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.210
try and get it into the frame, and all of

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.531
a sudden it goes yellow.

00:00:36.131 --> 00:00:40.196
[Description] When the pointer hovers over “NEWS”, the link turns pale yellow on white.

00:00:40.796 --> 00:00:43.636
But now the contrast ratio is bad enough that I

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:47.956
can't hardly tell what I'm looking at. That's a big,

00:00:47.956 --> 00:00:49.395
big sticking point.

00:00:49.395 --> 00:00:52.096
None of this is clickable at the moment, 'cause this

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:56.015
[Description] A notification popup has appeared: a dark square logo with the letter “C”, the

00:00:56.015 --> 00:00:59.933
text “Subscribe to our notifications and updates. You can disable anytime.”, a “Later” link

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:03.852
and a blue “Subscribe” button. Magnified, Justin sees only fragments of it at a

00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:07.770
time.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:15.030
popup has occurred. So it can be difficult. It's a

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.070
popup showing up on a web page, and you can't

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.030
get out of it, or you can't find it. This

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:27.910
is pretty confusing. The popup is only findable based on

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.829
this contrast here, between this and this. But otherwise it's

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:33.589
difficult to see it's even there.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:37.430
[Description] Justin moves the pointer onto “Later”, then zooms out to the whole page and

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.090
back in. Hovering over the “PEOPLE” link turns it yellow.

00:01:42.269 --> 00:01:44.429
So sometimes I'll be clicking around on a site and

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:47.510
I'm like, why is nothing working? And then I'm looking

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.590
around the page, I'm trying to figure out what's what,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.390
and I finally find that, oh, there's a popup. I

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:55.990
need to close that. And then things start functioning again.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.974
[Description] End card: the Perspective Tester logo.

